*.local
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor and tooling config, not part of the released tool.
.claude/

# Test harness output. Every `_*.ts` under app/tests is generated: the slices a
# suite writes to drive a module, and the esbuild ENTRY POINTS, which
# _combatdrive.mjs's loadCombat(name) writes with writeFileSync at the top of
# every run. There is no exception, and app/tests/.gitignore says the same thing
# closer to the files.
#
# EXACTLY ONE harness file under `_` is hand written — _combatdrive.mjs, the DOM
# shim and esbuild loader rejoin.test.mjs and surplusdefense.test.mjs import —
# and it is un-ignored below. An earlier pass here claimed three were, and that
# the two .entry.ts files "are rewritten by nobody"; both claims were wrong.
# Measured against a clean `git checkout-index` export: with _combatdrive.mjs
# present and the two entry files DELETED, rejoin is 27/27 and surplusdefense
# 16/16 and both entry files are back on disk afterwards; with _combatdrive.mjs
# deleted, ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND before a single assertion runs.
app/tests/_*.ts
# The bundles those entry points are built into are build artefacts too.
app/tests/_*.mjs
# The one negation that is real. Nothing deeper ignores .mjs, so this is the
# line that decides it.
!app/tests/_combatdrive.mjs

# Cached responses from the publisher's card API (tools/sync_official.mjs).
.cache/
